Source surface geodesic attribution and provenance

This TypeScript translation follows pmp::geodesics, the triangulated fast-marching solver with unfolded virtual edges used by the pinned GarmentMeasurements measurement program. It is not the heat-method solver and does not reconstruct original SMPL landmark assignments.

GarmentMeasurements repository commit: 04e9197c37197c5b05c1c86abf5ac503864e0d8f
Checked-in external/pmp-library tree: 5af8892e2530729ea07b8b20dca52f1be7afde29
pmp CMake version: 2.0.1 (the dependency is checked in; it has no separate submodule commit here).
geodesics.cpp SHA-256: 793e40aedc01fca2f7912a73fb77b661df693c37b09d6acd5bc5d775daa4686f
geodesics.h SHA-256: 6d0824a084c38b590c315de0c4cb8e60ac6d00f6d41faaa0de696776cff90fa2
Upstream URL: https://github.com/maria-korosteleva/GarmentMeasurements
Method reference: R. Kimmel and J. A. Sethian, Computing Geodesic Paths on Manifolds, PNAS 1998.

